WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.460
Silas Robertson — better known as Uncle
Si — has been entertaining people with his

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.480
quirks and hijinks since 2012, when he was
first featured on A&amp;E's Duck Dynasty reality

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:09.980
series.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.540
"I was a player before they even invented
the game, Jack."

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.960
Along with his ever-present iced tea glass,
he shot to household recognition and went

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.460
on to become the most popular person on the
show.

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:25.180
Uncle Si and his catchy sayings decorate many
a piece of Duck Dynasty merchandise, and he's

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.660
even received the coveted Chia Pet treatment.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.960
However, Duck Dynasty ended in April of 2017,
and Robertson retired from working at Duck

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.240
Commander, the duck-call manufacturing business
featured on the show.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.060
"Hey.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.140
I gotta clear my head."

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:43.040
So where is Si Robertson today, and what keeps
him entertained ever since he left the immediate

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.200
national spotlight?

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:48.400
As it turns out, Uncle Si is a jack of all
trades when it comes to hobbies: he's tried

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.320
his hand at writing, music-making, and, of
course, viral video analysis, which he conducted

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.030
alongside his nephew Willie Robertson on his
short-lived spin-off series Going Si-Ral that

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.100
wrapped shortly before Duck Dynasty did.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.340
Virtually the moment the show ended, Robertson
released a book in May 2017.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:09.860
Entitled Si-renity: How I Stay Calm and Keep
the Faith, the book is something of a behind-the-scenes-slash-memoir

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.390
that looks back at his entire life, including
his time spent on the A&amp;E reality show.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.700
But this was actually Robertson's fourth published
book.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.530
It came after Si-cology 1: Tales and Wisdom
from Duck Dynasty's Favorite Uncle and two

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.810
children's books, Uncle Si and The Christmas
Elf and Everything's Better with a Beard,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.880
which features the entire Robertson clan.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:33.060
Since then, Uncle Si has decided to lean full-tilt
into a music career by founding his own country

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.650
music group, Uncle Si and the Sicotics.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.799
The band consists of Robertson, his daughter-in-law
Marsha Robertson, and celebrated singer-songwriter

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.740
Bridgette Tatum.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:47.540
They recorded a single called "As Seen on
TV" in 2017, and subsequently released a self-titled

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.040
EP.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.960
Before the end of Duck Dynasty — and at
what was arguably the apex of his mainstream

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.159
fame — Robertson expanded his reach on the
small-screen by appearing on the television

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:00.909
series Last Man Standing, playing a character
called Uncle Ray opposite Tim Allen in the

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:02.979
2013 episode "Back to School."

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:07.409
He also dabbled in feature films, landing
a small part in the 2015 Christian religion

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.020
film Faith of Our Fathers.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.500
"Hey, this stuff is so good you'll punch your
momma."

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.460
He also lent his voice to narrate VeggieTales:
Merry Larry and the True Light of Christmas.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:20.590
However, the bite of the acting bug didn't
have long-lasting effects — Robertson hasn't

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:24.260
stepped in front of the camera since Duck
Dynasty ended in 2017.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.590
And it seems that won't change any time soon,
as his focus is on Uncle Si and the Sicotics.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.600
Robertson explained in a May 2018 interview
with Pop Culture that he had grown accustomed

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.709
to a certain way of life during the heyday
of Duck Dynasty, but he isn't about to let

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:41.959
a lack of riches keep him from a career in
music — something he had previously attempted

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.660
in 2014 with the release of his EP Me and
My Smokin' Hot Honey.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:46.400
He explained,

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.660
"I got to start making me some money somewhere.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.540
But I just chose the wrong industry to really
make a lot of money.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.740
I think there's a lot of goals that we want
to meet as a band.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.420
I would love to see that we finish this record
out, because I would love to see what we could

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.670
write beyond what we've got.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.180
I think everybody believes it to be just this
funny thing, and there's a lot of that on

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:02.680
there.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.700
But there's also some moments that happen
on there that are really important, and I

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.060
would love just to be able to have the opportunity
that we can all write together some more and

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.340
see how deep we can go."

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.860
Finishing a full-length album is the band's
current priority, as Uncle Si and the Sicotics

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.960
are no longer actively touring the country.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.720
If you want to keep tabs on them, they regularly
post videos on their Facebook page.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.500
Even though Duck Dynasty is over, Si Robertson's
life clearly hasn't stopped for a second.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.540
"Hey, when they say they don't know what hit
em, that's because it was me that hit em."

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.180
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.500
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

